+- Two homes of one enumerated list (here `publishingActions`: PRD AC-34.4 and ADR-4 preview) when the decisions-log "ответы пользователя" entry names both: user-approved, compare the copies for drift, do not raise the duplication.
+
+**Defect shapes that paid off:**
+- c4-full delta carrying a `desk.md` Purpose/Key paths proposal: the registry template excludes purpose and key paths, and ADR-1's hard-gate block already holds them (copies drift). Fixed by pointing to the ADR-1 block.
+- UX text catalog re-listing static mockup strings verbatim, against its own lede; route lists in both a UX decision and an ADR "final routes" table. After the trim, check the remaining catalog strings against the mockups word for word (iteration 2: "Вместе с версией" in the catalog vs "Вместе с ней" in two modals). An autofix that adds a catalog row can reintroduce static buttons and a string already in another row (iteration 3: «Не сейчас», «Утвердить вместе с {n} записями»): medium, so only raised while the floor is medium or lower.
+- DESIGN.md edits promised "at design-promote" in prose while no `design-md-delta.yaml` exists; once it exists, read it against `t_design-md-delta.yaml`: `new_value` must be the real token value (a sentinel like `"unchanged"` on a composite token breaks the patch) and `reason` is "why", not the table row to add.
+- Resolved hard-gate branches left in accepted ADRs (fallback variant, "if not approved"), and counts restating the list below them. A leftover can also be the cross-reference that outlives its own fix (ADR-6 "routes provisional in U-22" after U-22 was rewritten to delegate to ADR-6).
+- A sprint draft linking a sibling draft (`ux-spec.html` -> `adr.html#adr-6`): ADRs are never promoted standalone, so the link dangles in `docs/ux/`. Plain text or the fold-target doc instead.
+- One enumerated rule (here the four `publishingActions` cases, who-is-checked) restated across PRD ACs, UX notes and ADR: grep a distinctive phrase across all three drafts, then compare the copies - one has usually drifted.
+- A new AC added by an autofix: grep its id across ADR/UX. Iteration 3 left ADR-4 "Context" at "AC-34.1–34.9" and its decision item citing a neighbour id, and AC-34.7 rewritten to "an action not in this list publishes nothing" (reads wrongly for record approval). Both medium: raise only when the floor allows.
+- External-norm claims ("recommended by OWASP") without a source, against `design-principles.md` 11 (iteration 2 added source and date: accepted).
+
+**Why:** the finding rows are limited to one `f` per rubric row, so hang each finding on the row it fits best and merge same-kind drift; the decisions-log segments (`decisions-log.00N.md`, live `decisions-log.md`) are the evidence for dates and approvals. A new file in the iteration (the delta) is absent from the `.diff` - read it whole.
+
+**How to apply:** at design-review iteration 1 read each draft whole (no `.diff`); in later iterations read the hand-off `.diff` first, then whole files only for cross-checks. Check the iteration floor before deciding a shape is raisable (iteration 3-4: high only).
